0..75 Comment "/// Two transports in a variable family compare by their family, their path"
76..96 Comment "/// and their value."
97..100 Comment "///"
101..180 Comment "/// Each transport lowers its own motive, so the two motives are distinct terms"
181..257 Comment "/// that read one family. Each second value is a call, which the kernel runs"
258..287 Comment "/// before it reads the path."
288..291 Comment "///"
292..371 Comment "/// The rows transport along a variable path, along a variable function\'s path,"
372..413 Comment "/// and under a variable function\'s call."
414..417 Comment "///"
418..489 Comment "/// - see: #3802 — two motives calling one variable family read apart"
490..589 Comment "/// - see: #3806 — the checker compared the transports first, and the kernel refused its dialogue"
591..659 Comment "/// A definition that returns its argument, so a call to it unfolds."
